  "details": "Since build 1490, when the controller bindings system switched over to use SteamVR bindings, the option to manually set the action menu to be triggered by thumb stick clicks have disappeared.\n\nWhile it was annoying to go through the cryptic labels within the SteamVR bindings menu, I did manage to set it back to the same way I've used the action menu for years now, by setting thumb stick clicks to \"action_menu\". As far as I know, there is currently no other way to change that.\n\nToday, after build 1491 dropped, I am constantly getting the \"missing bindings\" error message every time I start up the game. To test my theory, I reset the bindings to the defaults, then *only* changed the thumb stick clicks to \"action_menu\". After restarting, I get the message again during startup.\n\nI'm not sure if this is a bug or a design oversight in this current build. Surely it wouldn't make sense to give end-users the option to customize the bindings to fit their comfort, only to bother them at every startup that their bindings are either broken or wrong?",
